      "content": "It's heartbreaking when the logic of the universe feels so cold compared to the pain of being human, but that effort you make to question things is actually proof that your humanity matters deeply. You don't have to \"fix\" this feeling immediately or convince the physical laws to change; sometimes the most rebellious act is just to rest and let the emotions wash over you without fighting them. Please remember that even if reality feels indifferent, the shared experience of trying to understand it connects you to others who feel the same weight.",
